[26.633506, "o", "R1_ARM=PC R1_ENTRY=coordinator R1_ROUTES=coordinator=cloud,implementor=local,verifier=local,plan=cloud,implement=local,critique=local,smol=local\r\n"]
[155.524991, "o", "```\r\n/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/\r\n  README.txt\r\n  pip-24.3.1.dist-info/    ← claims pip is installed\r\n                            ← no pip/ directory beside it\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo every entry point died with `/usr/local/bin/python3: No module named pip`, including the `/usr/local/bin/pip3` wrapper. That shape — `dist-info` present, package tree gone — is what an interrupted upgrade or uninstall leaves behind.\r\n\r\nI ruled the plausible alternatives out rather than assuming: no PEP 668 gate on this interpreter (the `EXTERNALLY-MANAGED` marker exists only for the distro 3.11 under `/usr/lib/python3.11/`), site-packages was writable, no `pip.conf` or `PIP_*` overrides, and a throwaway venv installed `six` from PyPI fine — so the index and network were never the problem.\r\n\r\n**The repair.** Moved the stale metadata aside and reinstalled pip from the wheel Python already ships, no network bootstrap:\r\n\r\n```\r\nmv .../site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info /tmp/pip-24.3.1.dist-info.stale-bak\r\npython3 -m ensurep"]
[155.52511, "o", "ip --upgrade --default-pip\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Proof it works**, not just that it imports — a real download and install:\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ python3 -m pip install --no-input six\r\nSuccessfully installed six-1.17.0\r\n$ python3 -m pip --version\r\npip 24.3.1 from /usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/pip (python 3.13)\r\n$ python3 -m pip check\r\nNo broken requirements found.\r\n```\r\n\r\nI checked this the hard way deliberately: my first verification was `pip install --dry-run pip`, which came back \"Requirement already satisfied\" and proved nothing, since it resolves locally without touching a download.\r\n\r\nWritten up in `docs/pip-repair.md`, including the ruled-out hypotheses table and a one-liner that spots this failure mode again in a single call.\r\n\r\nTwo things worth knowing:\r\n- `/tmp/pip-24.3.1.dist-info.stale-bak` is the old metadata, kept for recovery — safe to delete. `six` 1.17.0 is now installed system-wide as the proof; remove it if you don't want it.\r\n- Your distro Python 3.11 at `/usr/bin/python3.11` was untouched, and its p"]
[155.525137, "o", "ip is still absent — that was already true and I left it alone.\r\n\r\nFor project work, use a venv rather than system installs; this interpreter has no PEP 668 guard, so pip will happily let you modify the system site-packages.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=18 surface=61f55334a6b1\r\n"]
